@startuml
!include docs/uml/theme.puml
title ShadeNav Operational Architecture
left to right direction
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

' === External Actors ===
package "User" {
  actor "Young Pedestrian" as YoungPedestrian
  actor "Worker" as Worker
  actor "Parent\n(with kids)" as Parent
  actor "Courier\nby foot" as Courier
  actor "Tourist" as Tourist
}

package "External Data Sources" {
  entity "Map Services" as MapAPI
  entity "Meteo Sources" as Meteo
  entity "Local Open Data" as OpenData
}

' === System Components ===
package "SafeNav System" {
  component "UI Layer" as UI
  component "Routing Engine" as Router
  component "Context Analyzer" as Analyzer
}

' === Layout hints ===
' Keep data sources on the far right
' SafeNav System center
' User on far left
' (Use long arrows to show cross-package flow)

' === 1. User Interaction ===
User --> UI : Route request
User <.. UI : Route alternatives in map and scores

' === 2. Internal data and preferences ===
UI -r-> Router : Route start/end points
UI --> Analyzer : User preferences

' === 3. Route Computation ===
Router --> Analyzer : Possible routes (ETA + distance)

' === 4. External Data Retrieval ===
Router --> MapAPI : Request map
Router <.. MapAPI : Return map

Analyzer --> Meteo : Request weather data
Analyzer <.. Meteo : Return weather data

Analyzer --> OpenData : Request streets data
Analyzer <.. OpenData : Return streets data

Analyzer --> UI : Routes + Route scores


' === UI Note ===
note left of UI
Handles all user interactions:
• Trip definition (origin / destination)
• Display of route alternatives
• Route selection and guidance
UI may be web or mobile.
end note

note bottom of Router
Responsible for computing possible
routes between origin and destination
using map data.
end note

note top of Analyzer
Analyzes routes based on
environmental context (shade,
weather) and user preferences
to score and rank alternatives.
end note

@enduml
